ChatMeet – Child Sexual Abuse and Exploitation (CSAE) Policy

1. Our Commitment to Child Safety

ChatMeet is committed to maintaining a safe environment for all users. We have zero tolerance for Child Sexual Abuse and Exploitation (CSAE), Child Sexual Abuse Material (CSAM), child grooming, or any activity that exploits, abuses, or endangers children.

ChatMeet strictly prohibits the creation, uploading, sharing, requesting, promoting, or distribution of any content involving child sexual abuse or exploitation.

The safety and protection of children are among our highest priorities.

2. Adults-Only Platform (18+)

ChatMeet is exclusively intended for adults aged 18 years and older.

Individuals under the age of 18 are strictly prohibited from registering, accessing, or using ChatMeet.
Users must provide accurate age information during registration.
We reserve the right to suspend or permanently terminate accounts suspected of belonging to individuals under 18.
Users must not misrepresent their age or encourage minors to access the platform.
Reports of underage users will be reviewed and appropriate action will be taken.

Our age restrictions are intended to prevent minors from accessing or participating in our platform.

3. Prohibited Content and Activities

ChatMeet strictly prohibits:

Child Sexual Abuse Material (CSAM).
Sexual exploitation or abuse of minors.
Child grooming or attempts to establish inappropriate relationships with minors.
Sexual solicitation or inappropriate communication involving minors.
Sharing, requesting, creating, or distributing sexual images or videos involving children.
Encouraging, facilitating, or promoting child trafficking or exploitation.
Any behavior that sexually exploits, abuses, or endangers children.

Any violation of these standards may result in immediate account suspension or permanent termination.

4. Reporting and User Feedback

ChatMeet provides users with a mechanism to report inappropriate behavior, suspected CSAM, child exploitation, or other child safety concerns.

Users can report suspicious accounts or content through the reporting functionality available within the application.

We take all child safety reports seriously and will:

Review submitted reports promptly.
Investigate suspected violations.
Remove or restrict offending content where appropriate.
Suspend or permanently terminate accounts involved in violations.
Escalate confirmed cases to appropriate authorities when required by applicable laws.

Users are encouraged to report any suspected child exploitation or abuse immediately.

5. Content Moderation and Enforcement

ChatMeet is committed to taking appropriate action against content and activities involving child exploitation.

Our enforcement measures include:

Reviewing reports of suspected CSAE and CSAM.
Taking appropriate action when we obtain actual knowledge of prohibited content.
Removing confirmed violating content.
Suspending or permanently banning offending accounts.
Preventing repeat offenders from returning to the platform where reasonably possible.
Cooperating with relevant authorities and child protection organizations.

We maintain a zero-tolerance approach toward child sexual abuse and exploitation.

6. Reporting to Authorities

ChatMeet is committed to complying with applicable child safety laws and regulations.

When we identify or obtain actual knowledge of confirmed CSAM or child exploitation, we will take appropriate action and report the matter to the relevant authorities or child protection organizations, as required by applicable laws.

This may include the National Center for Missing & Exploited Children (NCMEC) or the appropriate regional reporting authority, depending on the applicable jurisdiction.

We will cooperate with legitimate law enforcement investigations and lawful requests for information.

7. Child Safety Point of Contact

ChatMeet has a designated child safety contact responsible for receiving communications concerning CSAE and CSAM prevention, enforcement, and compliance.

For child safety concerns, policy questions, or reports involving suspected child exploitation, please contact:

Child Safety Email: firebase.veltrixy@gmail.com

This contact is intended for child safety matters and communications from relevant authorities and organizations.

8. User Responsibility

All ChatMeet users are responsible for following this policy.

Users must not create, share, request, distribute, or encourage any material or behavior involving child sexual abuse or exploitation.

Users must report suspected violations and must not attempt to use ChatMeet to facilitate harmful activities involving children.

Violations may result in immediate account termination and reporting to the appropriate authorities where required.

9. Policy Enforcement

ChatMeet reserves the right to investigate suspected violations and take appropriate enforcement actions, including:

Removing prohibited content.
Suspending user accounts.
Permanently banning users.
Restricting access to platform services.
Reporting confirmed cases to relevant authorities.

We may update this policy as necessary to reflect changes in applicable laws, regulations, and child safety requirements.

10. Our Commitment

ChatMeet is committed to providing a safe, responsible, and lawful platform for adults.

We maintain zero tolerance for Child Sexual Abuse and Exploitation and continuously strive to strengthen our child safety practices.

By using ChatMeet, users agree to comply with these standards and understand that any involvement in child sexual abuse or exploitation is strictly prohibited.

